151 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 96 0 R/T(HELLO I am Vishakha Bharti a fourth year student doing my Bachelors in  architecture at IIT Kharagpur, and I am still learning what it means to truly listen to a space. Architecture, for me, is not simply about building \204 it is about understanding the quiet negotiations between people and the places they inhabit, between structure and sky, between what a site demands and what a person needs.)/E(HELLO I am Vishakha Bharti a fourth year student doing my Bachelors in  architecture at IIT Kharagpur, and I am still learning what it means to truly listen to a space. Architecture, for me, is not simply about building \204 it is about understanding the quiet negotiations between people and the places they inhabit, between structure and sky, between what a site demands and what a person needs.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

152 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 96 0 R/T(I am drawn to the moments where design becomes almost invisible \204 where a threshold feels natural, where light falls exactly as it should, where a room holds its occupant without announcing itself. I want to understand how those moments are made, and how to make them deliberately.)/E(I am drawn to the moments where design becomes almost invisible \204 where a threshold feels natural, where light falls exactly as it should, where a room holds its occupant without announcing itself. I want to understand how those moments are made, and how to make them deliberately.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

153 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 96 0 R/T(I sketch because thinking slows down when my hand moves. I observe because every built thing has an argument embedded in it. And I design because I believe that space, at its most honest, can hold the full complexity of a human life.)/E(I sketch because thinking slows down when my hand moves. I observe because every built thing has an argument embedded in it. And I design because I believe that space, at its most honest, can hold the full complexity of a human life.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[8]>>
