591 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 108 0 R/T(Kolkata, West Bengal)/E(Kolkata, West Bengal)/Pg 23 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

592 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 108 0 R/E(In a country where folk art does not hang in galleries but lives in the hands of the people who make it, this museum was designed to close that distance. Banglar Shilpo Ghar, the House of Bengal's Craft is rooted in the visual language of the land it celebrates: terracotta patterns borrowed from temple facades, bamboo screens that filter light the way a Kantha stitch filters colour, open courtyards that echo the rhythm of a village maidan.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

593 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 108 0 R/E(The building is organised around three galleries Folk Art, Folk Music, and Folk Handcraft each unfolding as a sensory journey rather than a simple display. Light, texture, sound, and material work together to create an experience that does not just show Bengali heritage but lets visitors feel its weight and warmth. This is a building that does not merely house culture it participates in it, quietly and with conviction.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

