3092 0 obj
<</Title(In a coastal city where the relationship between people and the sea is ancient and unhurried, this resort was designed not as an escape from place but as a deeper entry into it. Chennai's shoreline carries a particular quality of wind the Thendral that moves through coconut groves, fishing villages, and temple courtyards before it reaches the water's edge. This resort was designed to catch that wind deliberately, to let it move through every corridor, every verandah, every shaded outdoor space as though the building had always been a part of the landscape it sits within.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 3089 0 R/Next 3093 0 R>>
endobj

3093 0 obj
<</Title(Thendral Marabu is not simply a place to stay. It is an attempt to translate the rhythm of coastal Tamil heritage into built form where materiality, orientation, and spatial sequence together tell the story of a shoreline that has been lived in for centuries. A resort where arriving feels less like checking in and more like coming home to something you did not know you remembered.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 3089 0 R/Prev 3092 0 R>>
endobj

