3186 0 obj
<</Title(In a city that gathers to perform, to celebrate, to mourn, and simply to be together, the question this building asked was not how large a stage should be, but how generously a building can give itself to the people around it. The Sanskriti Milon Kendra begins as a single solid volume heavy, grounded, and certain and is then opened up strategically, carved away at its edges to create thresholds, courtyards, and passages that draw the public in before they have even bought a ticket.)/Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/Parent 3183 0 R/Next 3187 0 R>>
endobj

3187 0 obj
<</Title(The auditorium at its core is precise and acoustically resolved, designed for performance at the highest level. But wrapped around it is a porous public realm community gathering spaces, multipurpose halls, open display areas that ensures the building is alive even on the days when the stage is dark. Architecture here is not a backdrop for civic life. It is civic life, given form and permanence.)/Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/Parent 3183 0 R/Prev 3186 0 R>>
endobj

